      "association_text": "Prevotella copri caused a clinically significant bloodstream infection (bacteremia) in a 90-year-old male patient with acute cardiac decompensation due to heart failure, representing the first reported case of BSI attributed to this organism; blood cultures grew P. copri as the sole pathogen and the patient recovered following treatment with metronidazole and piperacillin-tazobactam.",
